Each verb is a whole step of a Discipline and refuses its own misuse
(solorepo's DR-116): a composition a caller could assemble by hand and leave
half done is not typeable here. The body is `.meta/lib/move/`, one module per
lifecycle (solorepo's DR-264): `common`, `challenges`, `pull_requests`, `decisions`,
`advance`, `manager`, `reconcile` and `cli`. This entry holds no logic
(solorepo's DR-217): it exports each module beside the names it defines, so a
caller reaches a verb by the script's own name and a probe reaches the seam
it stands in through the module. Two modules share a name with the verb
they hold, `advance` and `reconcile`, and there the name wins and the module
is reached by the package path or through a module that imports it, as
`manager` does `advance`. `channel`, which every module draws on, and
`check_pr`, which four of them do, are exported beside them as they always
were.

History in move.history.md (solorepo's DR-171).
"""
